<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nakhchivan Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhchivan</a> Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic was an autonomous republic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> SSR, created in 1924 for the Nakhchivan region, separated from the rest of Azerbaijan by Armenian territory. Its status followed the treaties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> of 1921, which placed it under Azerbaijan. In 1990 it became the Nakhchivan Autonomous Republic, which it remains within independent Azerbaijan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nakhchivan-autonomous-soviet-socialist-republic.jpg" alt="Nakhchivan Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ericmetro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Nakhichevan_ASSR_(1978%E2%80%931990).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
